# French Suite No. 5 in G major, BWV 816: Gavotte (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: a cheerful gavotte in cut time, two beats to the bar, each
# phrase starting on the half-bar upbeat as the dance requires. Quarter
# notes in the melody with eighth-note turns, over a bass that moves in
# quarters. Poised and light, not hurried.
#
# Time signature: 2/2 (C barred), 24 bars in the Mutopia score and in
# the MIDI, with a half-note upbeat (bar 24 is the matching half bar).
# The MIDI plays each half once.
#
# Repeats: both halves repeated from their upbeats, written out with
# play. About 3.3 KB.
#   Performed bars: A 0.5-8.5, A repeat 8.5-16.5 (score x is x+8),
#   B 16.5-32 (score x is x+8), B repeat 32-47.5 (score x is x+23.5).
#
# Tempo: half note = 80, 48 bars with repeats, about 1:12.
# Track times: Angela Hewitt (Hyperion) 1:13, about half = 79 with both
# repeats; Alessandra Artifoni 1:08, about 85; Glenn Gould (Sony) 0:40,
# about 72 if without repeats (not confirmed). 80 follows Hewitt.
#
# Structure (my reading of the Mutopia score):
#   1-4     G major, the theme from the upbeat; answer phrase to E minor.
#   5-8     to D major; cadence in D at 8.
#   9-12    D major, then toward E minor (dis, 12).
#   13-16   running eighths, cadence in E minor (16).
#   17-20   C major and A minor (F natural in 18).
#   21-24   home to G; the final cadence with its trill (23-24).
#
# Plan: each half full the first time and echoed on the repeat. In B
# the move through C major (score 17-20) steps down a level, then full
# for the return home.

pickup 2

tempo 80 2

play 0.5-8.5 0.5-8.5 8.5-24.5 8.5-24

dyn 1 f            # A first time, from the upbeat
dyn 8.5 mp         # A repeat, an echo
dyn 16.5 f         # B first time: D major to E minor
dyn 25 mf          # score 17-20: C major and A minor, a step down
dyn 29 f           # score 21-24: home to G
dyn 32 mp          # B repeat, an echo
dyn 44.5 f         # score 21 on: full for the close

rit 2 0.8          # the last two bars into the final G
